# Sixteen curated suites were never added to this allowlist, so the `test_*.py`
# rule above was silently ignoring them: test_cutscene.py alone is 50 tests
# encoding what two days of live renders taught us about the opening montage, and
# none of it could be committed. Found when `git show <sha>:test_cutscene.py` came
# back "exists on disk, but not in <sha>". They run and they belong in the repo.
!test_ceremony_hud.py
!test_coinop.py
!test_cutscene.py
